[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two stuffed beefsteak tomatoes are centered in the frame, angled at 3/4 overhead to showcase their volume and the vibrant filling within the hollowed cavities. The depth of field is shallow, keeping the foreground tomato crisp and the second tomato slightly softer in the background. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window to the left, casting gentle, natural shadows and creating a subtle sheen on the olive oil-slicked mackerel mixture. The tomatoes are bright red and firm, overflowing with a rustic, textured filling of flaky, pearly-white mackerel, creamy mashed cannellini beans, dark purple chopped Kalamata olives, and flecks of vibrant green flat-leaf parsley. A few stray bits of parsley and a small smear of olive oil are visible on the matte, off-white ceramic plates. Beside the plates, several golden-brown whole-wheat pita wedges are artfully arranged, showing a slight, natural tear in the crust. The setting is an aged oak wood table with visible grain and subtle wear marks. Props include a slightly used wooden spoon resting near the pita and a small ramekin containing a bit of leftover parsley, blurred in the background. The scene reflects a home-cooked, warm meal. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The arrangement is authentic, featuring slight imperfections like a small, realistic sauce drip on the plate rim and an asymmetric scatter of crumbs. No plastic sheen, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography for a high-end cookbook."
]
